  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The distance between two point charges, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q_{2}\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>. Point P is located on the straight line connecting the two charges, at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\"></span> from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q_{1}\"></span>. The electric potential due to the charges is a minimum at point P. What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{q_{2}}{q_{1}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{(x-a)^{2}}{a^{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{a^{2}}{(x-a)^{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x-a}{a}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{a}{x-a}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
